  "shortAnswer": "Missed stitches are almost always mechanical or compatibility issues, not “operator error.” Start with sponge bar (presser/pressure bar), then yarn, then indivicual needles—you’ll usually find the cause quickly.",
  "outcomeLine": "Once the sponge bar, yarn, and needles are working together, stitches knit cleanly and consistently—no gaps, no guesswork.",
